+# R-B06 stage 1 round 2 — independent evidence before author response
+
+Frozen at 2026-10-04 13:34:19 UTC, before reading repair-1 report, responses, verifier or formal repair text. Candidate `b1b09be809822ffa8ab79684589d104ec783095a`; author evidence `5059760ea678e3c21ce01a87a13317b5b6cc2e1d`. This is a fresh review of only GIR-FD82-A032/A033/A035/A036/A037/A038/C120. Prior six scoped approvals are evidence history, not transferred approval.
+
+Reference independently fixed in `/tmp/R-B06-reference`, outside the project Git, at `8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b`, tree `7589c800b61ba13a13040ed0d686979b80a84fd0`, clean. Static reading only; no reference program, Ruby, regex evaluator, behavioral model, solver, conversion or game was run. No source code is copied into this report.
+
+## Independent preconditions and expected distinctions
+
+| Finding | Fresh source reading | Independent expected result / required premise |
+|---|---|---|
+| A032 | Utilities 001:247–283; Settings:57 | Name maximum 10. First token must be nonempty and strictly shorter than maximum; trailing digit removal precedes retry. Equality at maximum is not accepted by the second candidate either: fallback capitalizes and truncates the full system username. Preserve `john doe2` → `John`; distinguish `abcdefghi1` → `Abcdefghi`, `abcdefgh1` → `Abcdefgh1`, `ABCDEFGHIJ1 MiX` → `Abcdefghij`. Normal player metadata/charset fixture; no host username read. |
+| A033 | Trainer_LoadAndNew:4–10,70–96,108–124; Overworld:637–646; Messages:4–6; Interpreter_Commands:128–135 | Unknown trainer type raises at lookup before partner vehicle cancellation. Non-debug missing tuple short-circuits to true. Debug missing tuple can prompt creation then still return false from the outer check; event termination depends on optional interpreter. Missing-tuple fixture rejects creation and has absent or normally functioning interpreter/query; do not claim all exceptions absent. |
+| A035 | PokemonStorage:178–203,148–176 | Target-party copy appends to current length after full guard and compacts, even with explicit target 0 or 5; source object remains. Normal party `[A]`, source B gives `[A,B]`. Automatic target selection and target-box explicit-slot behavior remain separate. Healing can precede a box write when enabled. |
+| A036 | PokemonStorage:231–251; Settings:220,222,225 | Current full box is attempted first, then boxes in ascending order from 0. With current 3 full, 0/1/3 full and only box 2 slot 0 free: box 2/current 2. If box 0 and 2 slot 0 are free: box 0/current 0, box 2 unchanged. Full storage can still heal before failure; success vectors require normal fixture and specified healing state. |
+| A037 | Utilities_Pokemon:78–90; Pokemon:682–685,1159–1225; Player_Pokedex:41–45,147–151,195–218 | Quiet addition prechecks full storage, creates/registers/records first moves, then uses storage only when party already has 6; party 5 instead appends sixth. AQ-04 must restore full-party premise; original WP26 already had that premise and must remain unchanged. Normal data and no external creation callbacks are essential; partial registration before a downstream exception is not transactional rollback. |
+| A038 | UI_Bag:479–520; Trainer:57–83; Item:189–197; items:2942–2950 | Give menu requires a nonempty non-egg party and a holdable item. Eggs only → no Give; egg plus HP-0 non-egg → Give for POTION. Later selected-egg defense is distinct from menu eligibility. Menu inspection does not consume items. |
+| C120 / N001 | UI_PokemonStorage:315–332,378–396,424–435,593–613,1020–1062; PokemonStorage:63–76,101–117 | Fresh background read mutates matching legacy string to integer, and unavailable integer to ordinary box fallback, before bitmap display. Ruby `^`/`$` are line anchors, not absolute string anchors. Box 5 with `box2` followed by LF U+000A must normalize record/display to 2; `prefix` + LF + `box2` likewise; first matching line wins if several lines match. `box2x` has no such match: do not promise successful display or rollback if downstream type/asset handling fails. Nil/empty use display fallback without stored write. Re-lock does not promise reread when cached value is unchanged. Normal complete UI/asset fixture and exit-not-rollback memory premise remain. |
+| N002 | Trainer_LoadAndNew full static file, actual 124 lines | Old reported 1–135 exceeds EOF; truncated slice hash cannot validate its bounds. Correct successor must report 1–124 and reject invalid endpoints/order before any range hash. Test document validation only, never execute reference behavior. Preserve historical erroneous receipt with explicit successor correction. |
+
+Ruby anchor meaning checked against primary documentation: [Ruby 3.1 Regexp anchors](https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/3.1/Regexp.html#class-Regexp-label-Anchors). All behavioral expectations above are static inferences from the fixed source, not observed runs.
+
+## Dependency boundary to recheck in the candidate
+
+No write-path intersection alone proves independence. A032 metadata/charset access can read vehicle state; A033 partner and event-interpreter paths can touch B03-related helpers. The seven supported claims require their stated normal/absent helper fixtures. A035/A036 storage has healing and capacity premises; A037 construction, Pokédex and form callbacks require normal fixtures; A038 reads actual non-egg eligibility; C120 display caching and bitmap prerequisites limit the read/write claim. None of these seven requires the unresolved acquisition/evolution/move teaching propositions of A034/A059/C103. Their text, shared B05 CI/HP rows and unaccepted B03 input identities must be checked afresh.
+
+Remain outside approval: A034/A059/C103 until actually accepted B03 integration and new freeze; original/clean WP66-B complete C120 remains B16; runtime observations 0, proven demo chains 0, all static behavioral vectors unexecuted; U01–U10/G01–G12/AX01–AX20 and named unknowns retained. Public registration remains a suggestion, with no ID closure or whole-B06 READY.
